#lang r7rs
;; docs/archive/r7rs-dynamic-environment-shared-across-threads.md, for
;; fibers: the dynamic environment belongs to the code that is running, so a
;; fiber carries its own from yield to yield and from thread to thread
;; (tur_fiber_block_resume swaps it with the escapes).  Six fibers on a
;; three-thread scheduler, each inside its own parameterize, yield inside a
;; guard, a handler and the parameterize itself; 120 a fiber when each sees
;; only its own.  Afterwards the parameter reads its global value again.
(import (scheme base) (scheme write) (dynfwork) (turmeric dynfcrew))
(dynf-run)
(write (list 'fibers (dynf-total) 'outside (param-outside)))
(newline)
